Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Conformance fixtures: correct the replay, sender-identity
 and stale-head spec_gaps

StegVerse-Labs/.github#3369. Three spec_gap labels in the Protocol v1
conformance fixtures named the wrong defect or the wrong owner.

n2 (REPLAY): idempotent redelivery is the specified behaviour -- the I-10
ruling in docs/STEGDB_ORGANIZATION_ROLE_VERSION_PROPAGATION_MIRROR_HANDOFF.md,
partial-commit completion from the retained repository receipt, and
consume_outbox's exact-retry redelivery all depend on it -- so a missing
"replay refusal" is not a gap. n2 is now COVERED_WITH_SPEC_GAP: it covers
"no duplicate effect" at both ledger levels, and its gap is
REDELIVERY_REPROCESSED_BEFORE_DEDUPLICATION: receive() calls cross(), and so
the endpoint, before the recorded-transition lookup.

n3 (FORGED_IDENTITY): device or node attestation is prohibited as a gate
(device_attestation_gate NONE_PROHIBITED,
NO_DEVICE_ATTESTATION_OR_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_IDENTITY_GATE). The gap is now
SUBMITTER_KV_SKAP_VERIFICATION_NOT_BOUND_AT_INGRESS, owned by
SDK-MANIFEST-ECOSYSTEM-TRANSITION-DISPOSITION-001 with the KV/SKAP manifest
binding field owned by STEGOS-DEVICE-KV-SKAP-ROUNDTRIP-001, and its next step
binds workers/device_kv_skap_roundtrip_verifier.py receipts to the manifest.

n4 (STALE_HEAD_OR_FENCE): owned by the Registry/WorkerCoordinator owner per
the #3369 assignment, with organization ledger readback owned by
ORGANIZATION-BATCH-CUSTODY-REPLAY-001. CANONICAL-NODE-INGRESS-CONTRACT-001 is
a contract document, not a registered task.

The fixture test now also checks that every registered task id an owner
field names exists in data/canonical-task-records/, and that no gap waits on
an attestation owner. Generated expectations are unchanged.

